00:20:38.880 --> 00:20:44.960
a,000, then 1,500, then 2,000. Believe

00:20:42.320 --> 00:20:47.120
it or not, these graduated payments go a

00:20:44.960 --> 00:20:50.000
really, really long way at showing

00:20:47.120 --> 00:20:52.480
legitimacy and goodwill to the seller.

00:20:50.000 --> 00:20:54.240
aka you're showing them from month one

00:20:52.480 --> 00:20:56.080
that you're not a scam. And I really

00:20:54.240 --> 00:20:58.240
mean this in the context of comparing

00:20:56.080 --> 00:21:00.159
this to a deal where you make no

00:20:58.240 --> 00:21:01.600
payments for the first 6 months, right?

00:21:00.159 --> 00:21:03.280
He's going to have some heartburn about

00:21:01.600 --> 00:21:04.720
that because he probably doesn't know

00:21:03.280 --> 00:21:07.039
you all that well. And he's not going to

00:21:04.720 --> 00:21:09.360
know for 6 months if you're actually a

00:21:07.039 --> 00:21:11.360
good honest person yet or at least if

00:21:09.360 --> 00:21:13.200
you're going to do to this business or

00:21:11.360 --> 00:21:14.640
real estate what you say you're going to

00:21:13.200 --> 00:21:15.760
do. You're going to add value. You're

00:21:14.640 --> 00:21:17.360
going to improve it. He won't know that

00:21:15.760 --> 00:21:19.520
for six months. So, if you're having

00:21:17.360 --> 00:21:22.000
trouble with the trust part of a seller

00:21:19.520 --> 00:21:24.240
financing structure like this, then

00:21:22.000 --> 00:21:26.320
suggest graduated payments because they

00:21:24.240 --> 00:21:28.000
can almost have the same purpose, which

00:21:26.320 --> 00:21:30.159
is to save you money in your payments

00:21:28.000 --> 00:21:32.320
upfront, but it can go a really, really

00:21:30.159 --> 00:21:34.640
long way at buying some goodwill. Okay.

00:21:32.320 --> 00:21:36.799
The next structure is called a partial

00:21:34.640 --> 00:21:38.000
seller carryback. Now, this is called a

00:21:36.799 --> 00:21:40.000
half a dozen different things. That's

